# K03 NS-ROLES-2 REQUIRED POSITIVE, red until its dependency is built (Codex K03-NS2-COVERAGE-20261007-21,
# K03-NS2-COPY-ORACLE-20261007-22; steps/defects.md#named-body-copy-field).
# `box: merge: Inner` in Host's body is merge run when Host runs (docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#construction: declaring Host
# runs nothing of its body; #composition: merge copies its live operand), its result received in box
# (#explicit-copying); Host's later statements write through box and report through Out's declared fields.  Not read
# here: whether box is addressable from outside as Host\box (LMX_blog/q/q53.md, a computed receiver's output is not
# data; the generic RECEIVE-OUTPUT).  Today: "a merge construction in the body of a named Structure is not built yet".
# Exit 7; 80 if Host's body ran before its call, 81 if the copy did not read Inner's value of that moment, 82 if the
# write through box did not land, 83 or 84 if it reached Inner (box Inner itself), 85 if a second run did not copy again.
Inner:
    int: v 1
end: Inner
Out:
    int: first 0
    int: after 0
    int: inner 0
end: Out
Host:
    box: merge: Inner
    Out\first: box\v
    box\v: 5
    Out\after: box\v
    Out\inner: Inner\v
end: Host
fn: m () int
    Inner\v: 3
    if: Out\first != 0
        return: 80
    Host()
    if: Out\first != 3
        return: 81
    if: Out\after != 5
        return: 82
    if: Out\inner != 3
        return: 83
    if: Inner\v != 3
        return: 84
    Inner\v: 4
    Host()
    if: Out\first != 4
        return: 85
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
